			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add action-button Items field to ShowMessageRequest\n\nExtend the ShowMessageRequest protobuf message with a repeated `Items` string field to carry optional action-button labels alongside the message text. This allows Mountain-side callers (or Cocoon) to present a message with user-selectable actions, enabling confirmation dialogs, choice prompts, and interactive notifications over the gRPC channel.\n\nThe generated Rust code in `Source/Generated/vine.rs` is regenerated from the proto, adding the `items: Vec<String>` field to the `ShowMessageRequest` struct with the corresponding prost annotation and wire tag.\n\nThe field is optional (empty vector) by default, preserving backward compatibility with existing callers that only send a plain message.",
			"SHA": "a45249b1fdff37a15e592184cfbfbdc9c096b9f2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:35:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2514,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Polish README formatting, emoji annotations, and badge cleanup\n\nReplace the grape emoji 🍇 with herb 🌿 to better represent Vine's role as the protocol layer (a vine plant rather than a fruit). Add emoji annotations (⛰️🦋🪁🌳) alongside every component reference — Mountain, Cocoon, Air, Grove — so readers visually associate names with roles at a glance. Add `title=\"Star\"` attribute to the GitHub stars badge for accessibility.\n\nRemove the standalone gRPC/tonic badge line (the crate badges already indicate the gRPC and tonic dependency; the removed badge duplicated information while occupying a full row). Add a CHANGELOG link to the Related Documentation section and add Grove to the sibling-project references so the complete component set is cross-linked.\n\nStrip `&#x2001;` spacing tokens from Mermaid diagram node labels (they are not rendered by the diagram engine and clutter the source). Remove the duplicate 'Project Maintainers' footer block at the very end of the file — the funding/attribution table above it already covers project stewardship.\n\nApply consistent backtick formatting to technology names throughout: `gRPC`, `tonic`, `Prost`, `Node.js`, `WASM`, `Tauri`. Rewrap paragraphs to a consistent width for readability.\n\nThe README now presents a cleaner, more scannable architectural reference with emoji-aided navigation and deduplicated metadata.",
			"SHA": "d6ba6a4c3edd34c739bf071999215b0d25a26403"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:16:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2514,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Vine): Cap retry backoff, evict dead clients, fix lost-wakeup\n\nClamp exponential retry backoff to 5 s (MAX_BACKOFF_MS) in\nConnectToSideCar to prevent the doubling series from reaching ~102 s at\nattempt 9, which would hold boot for over 3 min on a dead sidecar.\n\nEvict the pooled gRPC client from SIDECAR_CLIENTS in RecordSideCarFailure\nonce the failure count passes MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS, so the next caller\nreceives ClientNotConnected and triggers a fresh reconnect instead of\nhammering a dead channel.\n\nPin max_decoding_message_size and max_encoding_message_size on the\nCocoonClient in TryConnectSingle to match ValidateMessageSize, ensuring\nthe wire bound is enforced before the codec round-trip.\n\nAdd ReportNotificationLag to surface broadcast channel subscriber drops\nthat would otherwise be silently lost.\n\nRewrite WaitForClientConnection from a single notified() await to a\nshort-slice polling loop with RECHECK_INTERVAL_MS = 100 ms. The re-check\ncloses the lost-wakeup window: notify_waiters only wakes waiters already\nregistered, so a waiter that subscribes after the handshake fired would\notherwise block for the entire budget even though the client is in the\npool.",
			"SHA": "81fc9d9313aff8d261d7d46c40d661600803062b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:38:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2514,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Standardize doc frontmatter and repository references\n\nDrop the introductory 'This document describes' framing from both Architecture.md and DeepDive.md in favour of direct statements that present Vine as the protocol layer itself rather than a document describing it. This aligns with the README's architectural-reference style established in cf60c5f.\n\nAdd a standardised project-maintainer footer to DeepDive.md matching the one in Architecture.md. Normalise email domain to `Editor.Land` (uppercase L) and redirect issue/repository URLs from the standalone `CodeEditorLand/Vine` repo to the monorepo `CodeEditorLand/Land`, reflecting Vine's current home as a submodule within the Land monorepo.",
			"SHA": "7ea3c3858ede7d439da6ae817f6b7144d47822ae"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:23:39Z",
